Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["ClassConfidence", "ObjectName",
 CellID->127261695,ExpressionUUID->"b1f6e274-82c3-924f-86ea-90c8ed8c372d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"924de5c0-457d-9a4f-9bce-3ef4661bb7f5"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["ClassConfidence",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:QMRIToolsNeuralNetworkTools/ref/ClassConfidence"], "[", 
   StyleBox["probability", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4408123b-d06a-d447-a541-119302b51588"],
 "\[LineSeparator]gives the confidence of a probability vector as produced by \
a network's softmax output, i.e. the same input ClassDecoder takes, without \
collapsing it to a class label. Confidence is 1 minus the normalized entropy \
of the vector, so it is 1 for a fully certain (one-hot) vector and 0 for a \
maximally uncertain (uniform) vector."
}], "Usage",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9981148195311737`*^9},
 CellID->238334616,ExpressionUUID->"9358df2d-893c-fa4d-a3ad-80e193c2b50f"],

